IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT math

-- Part 7 of the Legislation Interpretation Act 2021 (South Australia): time, distance, age and amounts.
-- Sections 44, 46 and 49 are time rules and are encoded in sa-interpretation-time.l4.
-- This module encodes sections 45, 47, 48 and 50.

§ `Part 7 -- Time, distance, age and amounts (sections 45, 47, 48 and 50)`

§§ `45 -- References to time`

-- src:535 | A reference in an Act or a legislative instrument to time in relation to doing anything in this or any other jurisdiction is a reference to the legal time in the jurisdiction.
@ref s 45 (src:535)
GIVEN `the reference is to time in relation to doing anything in this or any other jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the reference is a reference to the legal time in the jurisdiction` MEANS
    IF `the reference is to time in relation to doing anything in this or any other jurisdiction` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `47 -- References to number of sitting days`

-- A sitting day carries the session and the Parliament it fell in, because the rule says these do not matter.
DECLARE `Sitting day of a House` HAS
    `the day`    IS A DATE
    session      IS A NUMBER
    parliament   IS A NUMBER

GIVEN sitting IS A `Sitting day of a House`
      `the first day of the span` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the span` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a sitting day falls in the span` MEANS
    (Day (sitting's `the day`)) AT LEAST (Day `the first day of the span`)
    AND (Day (sitting's `the day`)) AT MOST (Day `the last day of the span`)

-- src:539 | A reference in an Act or a legislative instrument to a number of sitting days of a House of Parliament is, unless the contrary intention appears, a reference to the number of those days regardless of whether the days or some of the days occur in different sessions of Parliament or in different Parliaments.
@ref s 47 (src:539)
GIVEN `the sitting days` IS A LIST OF `Sitting day of a House`
      `the first day of the span` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the span` IS A DATE
      `the contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the number of sitting days in a span` MEANS
    IF `the contrary intention appears` THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (count (filter (`in the span`) `the sitting days`))
    WHERE
        `in the span` sitting MEANS `a sitting day falls in the span` sitting `the first day of the span` `the last day of the span`

§§ `48 -- Measuring distance`

DECLARE `Point` HAS
    east    IS A NUMBER
    north   IS A NUMBER
    height  IS A NUMBER

-- src:541 | In measuring a distance for the purposes of an Act or a legislative instrument, the distance is to be measured in a straight line on a horizontal plane.
@ref s 48 (src:541)
GIVEN `the first point` IS A `Point`
      `the second point` IS A `Point`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the distance measured in a straight line on a horizontal plane` MEANS
    SQRT (  ((`the second point`'s east MINUS `the first point`'s east) TIMES (`the second point`'s east MINUS `the first point`'s east))
          PLUS ((`the second point`'s north MINUS `the first point`'s north) TIMES (`the second point`'s north MINUS `the first point`'s north)))

§§ `50 -- Rounding down of monetary amounts`

-- src:546 | An Act or a legislative instrument providing for the calculation and payment of a tax, fee, charge or other amount must be construed as if it provided that the calculated amount, if not an exact multiple of 5 cents, is to be rounded down to the highest multiple of 5 cents that is less than that amount.
@ref s 50 (src:546)
GIVEN `the Act or instrument provides for the calculation and payment of a tax, fee, charge or other amount` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the calculated amount in cents` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the amount payable after rounding down to a multiple of 5 cents` MEANS
    IF `the Act or instrument provides for the calculation and payment of a tax, fee, charge or other amount`
    THEN JUST (5 TIMES (FLOOR (`the calculated amount in cents` DIVIDED BY 5)))
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Tests`

#ASSERT `the reference is a reference to the legal time in the jurisdiction` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the reference is a reference to the legal time in the jurisdiction` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Two sessions of one Parliament and a third day in the next Parliament: all four days count.
#ASSERT `the number of sitting days in a span` (LIST (`Sitting day of a House` OF (Date 3 3 2026), 1, 55), (`Sitting day of a House` OF (Date 4 3 2026), 1, 55), (`Sitting day of a House` OF (Date 5 8 2026), 2, 55), (`Sitting day of a House` OF (Date 9 3 2027), 1, 56)) (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 31 12 2027) FALSE EQUALS JUST 4
#ASSERT `the number of sitting days in a span` (LIST (`Sitting day of a House` OF (Date 3 3 2026), 1, 55), (`Sitting day of a House` OF (Date 4 3 2026), 1, 55), (`Sitting day of a House` OF (Date 5 8 2026), 2, 55), (`Sitting day of a House` OF (Date 9 3 2027), 1, 56)) (Date 4 3 2026) (Date 5 8 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST 2
#ASSERT `the number of sitting days in a span` (LIST (`Sitting day of a House` OF (Date 3 3 2026), 1, 55), (`Sitting day of a House` OF (Date 5 8 2026), 2, 55)) (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 31 12 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the number of sitting days in a span` (LIST (`Sitting day of a House` OF (Date 3 3 2026), 1, 55)) (Date 1 1 2027) (Date 31 12 2027) FALSE EQUALS JUST 0
-- 3 east, 4 north: a 5 metre line on the horizontal plane, whatever the difference in height.
#ASSERT `the distance measured in a straight line on a horizontal plane` (Point OF 0, 0, 0) (Point OF 3, 4, 0) EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `the distance measured in a straight line on a horizontal plane` (Point OF 0, 0, 0) (Point OF 3, 4, 120) EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `the distance measured in a straight line on a horizontal plane` (Point OF 10, 10, 5) (Point OF 10, 10, 50) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the distance measured in a straight line on a horizontal plane` (Point OF 0, 0, 0) (Point OF 0, 12, 0) EQUALS 12
#ASSERT `the amount payable after rounding down to a multiple of 5 cents` TRUE 2307 EQUALS JUST 2305
#ASSERT `the amount payable after rounding down to a multiple of 5 cents` TRUE 2305 EQUALS JUST 2305
#ASSERT `the amount payable after rounding down to a multiple of 5 cents` TRUE 2304 EQUALS JUST 2300
#ASSERT `the amount payable after rounding down to a multiple of 5 cents` TRUE 4 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `the amount payable after rounding down to a multiple of 5 cents` TRUE 5 EQUALS JUST 5
#ASSERT `the amount payable after rounding down to a multiple of 5 cents` TRUE 12.5 EQUALS JUST 10
#ASSERT `the amount payable after rounding down to a multiple of 5 cents` FALSE 2307 EQUALS NOTHING
